  "body": "Follow-up from the takeover of PR #3059 (#2988).\n\nIn `chamfer_open_runs` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/chamfer.rs`), the refusal `GenError::Empty(\"a chamfer edge holds a collapsed segment\")` runs after `simple()`. `simple()` already drops points closer than 1e-9 and refuses a run with fewer than two points. So with finite input the collapsed-segment refusal cannot fire.\n\nThe refusal that the user sees is the message of `simple()`: \"a centerline run needs at least two points\". For a chamfer, the word \"centerline\" is wrong.\n\nWork:\n1. Give the chamfer path its own message for a run that collapses (for example \"a chamfer edge collapses to one point\").\n2. Remove the dead check, or keep it as a guard with a comment that says why.\n3. Update the pin in `crates/motion/tests/chamfer_open_refusals.rs` to the new message.\n",
